#. Description of the plugin
msgid "Set a default block pattern for any post type's new-post editor. Patterns saved in the Site Editor take priority over patterns in code."
msgstr ""

#. Author of the plugin
msgid "Trent Stromkins"
msgstr ""

#. Author URI of the plugin
msgid "https://github.com/bmx269"
msgstr ""

#: pattern-primer.php:88
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr ""

#: pattern-primer.php:90
msgid "Build a pattern. Create one in the Site Editor (Appearance > Editor > Patterns), or use one that your theme or a plugin registers in code."
msgstr ""

#: pattern-primer.php:91
msgid "Enter its slug next to a post type on this screen. Start typing to see suggestions, then save."
msgstr ""

#: pattern-primer.php:92
msgid "Create a new post of that type. The editor opens with the pattern's blocks already in place."
msgstr ""

#: pattern-primer.php:94
msgid "Leave a post type blank to keep the normal empty editor. Only new posts that start out empty are filled, so existing content is never changed."
msgstr ""

#: pattern-primer.php:101
msgid "How matching works"
msgstr ""

#: pattern-primer.php:102
msgid "When a new post is created, the slug is looked up in this order and the first match is used:"
msgstr ""

#: pattern-primer.php:104
msgid "A published pattern saved in the Site Editor with that slug."
msgstr ""

#: pattern-primer.php:105
msgid "A pattern registered in code with that full name, such as mytheme/staff-profile."
msgstr ""

#: pattern-primer.php:106
msgid "A pattern registered in code whose name ends with the slug, such as staff-profile."
msgstr ""

#: pattern-primer.php:108
msgid "The Status column shows which one matched. \"Saved in Site Editor\" patterns have an Edit link. \"In Code\" patterns come from your theme or a plugin and are changed in their files."
msgstr ""

#: pattern-primer.php:113
msgid "More help"
msgstr ""

#: pattern-primer.php:114
msgid "Support forum"
msgstr ""

#: pattern-primer.php:115
msgid "GitHub"
msgstr ""

#: pattern-primer.php:190
msgid "Start every new post from the block pattern you picked for its post type."
msgstr ""

#: pattern-primer.php:199
msgid "Choose a pattern for each post type. New posts of that type open with its blocks already in place. Leave a field empty to keep the normal empty editor."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: example Saved Pattern slug, 2: example registered pattern name.
#: pattern-primer.php:204
msgid "Use the slug of a pattern saved in the Site Editor (%1$s) or the name of a pattern registered in code by your theme or a plugin (%2$s). Start typing to see suggestions. If both match, the pattern saved in the Site Editor takes priority over the one in code."
msgstr ""

